# Licensing

This repository uses a **dual license** depending on the type of content.

| Content type | License | File |
|---|---|---|
| **Code** — `*.py`, `*.js`, `*.ts`, `*.sh`, source under `practices/`, scripts, configs | **MIT License** | [`LICENSE-CODE`](./LICENSE-CODE) |
| **Documentation** — `*.md` files, notes, surveys, READMEs, articles, diagrams | **CC BY 4.0** | [`LICENSE-DOC`](./LICENSE-DOC) |

## Quick summary

- **Code (MIT)**: you may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,
  and sell, provided you include the copyright notice and this permission notice.
- **Docs (CC BY 4.0)**: you may share and adapt the documentation for any purpose,
  even commercially, provided you give appropriate credit and indicate changes.

## Third-party materials

Paper PDFs, slides, figures and any other third-party materials keep their
**original authors' copyright** and are collected here for research and
learning purposes only. Please refer to the original sources for licensing.

## How to attribute

When reusing this repository's content, please credit:

